//   intermediates do day to day signing): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Certificate_authority ; certificate revocation list (revoked
//   before scheduled expiry and should no longer be trusted): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Certificate_revocation_list ; OCSP (an
//   alternative to CRLs for revocation status): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Online_Certificate_Status_Protocol ; key ceremony
//   (generation may require witnesses and key holders present): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_ceremony
// Disk encryption (protects data at rest; a machine already running exposes its keys in memory):
//   https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disk_encryption
// Data loss prevention (data in motion across networks, at rest in storage, in use on endpoints; relies on classification; false
//   positives overwhelm review): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_loss_prevention_software
// Cloud computing (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS; customers have more control and responsibility in IaaS, less in PaaS and SaaS; hybrid):
